WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.483 --> 00:00:01.885
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.885 --> 00:00:02.970
(hockey sticks hitting)

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:03.803
- [Marissa] When we were younger,

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:06.320
I never thought I looked
any different than her.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:07.153
- [Hannah] And we didn't understand

00:00:07.153 --> 00:00:09.050
why people would be like,
"Are you actually sisters?"

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.910
We were like, "Yeah, obviously."

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.493
(upbeat music)

00:00:17.608 --> 00:00:20.800
(sticks hitting puck)

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.980
- My name's Hannah Brandt,
and I play for Team USA.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.900
- My name's Marissa Brandt, and
I play for Team South Korea.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:26.910
- And we're sisters.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.410
- [Marissa] I was born
in Seoul, South Korea,

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:33.340
and I was adopted when
I was four months old.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.410
I flew on a plane to the States

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:38.130
and that's where I met my parents.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.850
I started playing hockey when I was eight.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.240
And you started...

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:45.960
- I started when I was
about five years old.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.940
- [Marissa] We did everything
together growing up,

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.520
so really I chose hockey just
to be able to be with her,

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.660
but as I got older, I really
learned to love this sport.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.880
- [Hannah] We've played
together through high school

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.180
and then we went our
separate ways for college.

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:03.930
When we're on opposite ends of the world.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.740
- [Marissa] Everyday we
talk and text and ask

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:09.390
about how each other's days
went and games and whatnot

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:13.530
so yeah, I mean being so far
away we stay connected somehow.

00:01:14.816 --> 00:01:16.830
(crowd cheers)

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.410
- [Hannah] I think it's a super cool thing

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.270
that we're both going to the Olympics,

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:22.480
playing for different teams and in

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.790
the same sport I don't
know how common that is

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:28.160
so I think it makes it that
much more special for us

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.010
but I think for our family and friends,

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:32.180
that they have two teams to root for.

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:36.230
Just so happy to be able to
continue to play the sport

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:39.884
I love and be able to go to
the Olympics with this one.

00:01:39.884 --> 00:01:43.070
(happy music)

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:46.240
- [Marissa] Hockey has
shaped and influenced both

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:49.960
of our lives growing up so I
can't imagine a better reason

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.870
to be able to go back to my
home country, through hockey.

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:55.690
- [Hannah] For me going to
the Olympics has kinda always

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:57.600
been a dream of mine and then to be able

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.260
to watch my sister do the same thing

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:01.240
and to be able to go
through this experience

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.990
with her is just a dream come true.

00:02:03.881 --> 00:02:06.464
(happy music)

